c multiplicity of $\\lambda .$\n\nIn the characteristic polynomial\n\n$$\np(\\lambda )=(\\lambda +1)^{3}(\\lambda -3)^{2}(\\lambda +2)^{4},\n$$\n\nwe see that the root $\\lambda =-1$ has multiplicity $3.$ So the algebraic multiplicity of the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1$ is $3.$\n\nHowever, there are only $2$ eigenvectors corresponding to  the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1,$ so the geometric multiplicity of the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1$ is $2.$\n\nTherefore, the number of generalized eigenvectors of rank greater than $1$ corresponding to $\\lambda =-1$ is $3-2=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386446 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386446 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386448 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386446 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386449 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386446 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386446 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386446 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386446 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386446 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186386449 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386446 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "480350c9-2945-54c3-8987-b479d87ce01c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386447 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386447 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386447 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "195c4aec-4206-524d-999f-7c4101d2d7fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386448 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386448 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386448 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ba293136-d659-561c-8537-09a5722e5b25" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386449 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386449 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186386449 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "96a612d3-8f1e-5786-ae51-b97758955c46" #ed